--TEST--
`Core\Request::files` is the one member an uploaded part is received through: the walk binds a `Core\Request\Part` and no other body reader can be bound as one — `rule:http-server/an-upload-is-received-only-through-files` and `rule:http-server/a-part-is-a-file-iff-it-carries-a-filename`, `rule:security/request-state-throws-in-an-isolate`, spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:http-server/an-upload-is-received-only-through-files`'s governing sentence is "there is one way to receive it", and
// the depth shape is *agreement*: the same binding is asked of every member
// that can answer for a request body, so a second route to a part — a `post()`
// that quietly carried file fields, a `body()` that could be walked as parts —
// fails here while each member still reads plausibly on its own line.
//
// The superglobal half of the same rule is `a-superglobal-is-refused-and-names
// -its-core-class` (`rule:security/request-state-throws-in-an-isolate`); what is left to pin is that the `Core`
// surface which replaced it has one door and not two.
//
// The line that is *not* in the error list below is the assertion. The walk
// binds `Core\Request\Part` and compiles, so the file's only refusals are the
// two other readers — and a case that merely refused everything would report
// three.
foreach (Core\Request::files() as Core\Request\Part $part) {
    echo $part->name();
}

// § 2: form fields and file parts are separated by the same parse, and `post()`
// answers only the former. Its `?tainted string` is a form value, never a part.
Core\Request\Part $viaPost = Core\Request::post("upload");

// § 3: the raw body is the bytes, undivided. A program that wants the parts
// asks the member that yields them rather than re-deriving them from here,
// which is the whole reason `bodyStream` and `files` are two members.
Core\Request\Part $viaBody = Core\Request::body();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Request\Part`, found `null|tainted string`
%A
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Request\Part`, found `tainted string`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
